+# Delivery Note Details — FRO-361
+
+Unmounted read-only UI composition. Import DeliveryNoteDetails from components/delivery-note-details.tsx. This is UI preparation, not a live page or completed FRO-361 delivery.
+
+## Host contract
+
+Pass a discriminated state: loading, unavailable, error, or ready with DeliveryNoteDetailsModel. Non-ready states render no record data. Host must clear the old model while fetching a different identity or when access is lost.
+
+The model contains the existing DeliveryNote type, explicit shipmentReference and invoicingCompanyName display values, canOpenShipment, and hasSavedDraft. Display values are not invented API fields. Use the dedicated authorized single-note read once delivered; the existing Shipment list read excludes cancelled notes and is not a substitute.
+
+For a draft, hasSavedDraft must preserve the Shipment screen's shared saved-movement check across its current-note set, not merely the selected note. Supply false until that context is known. The component reuses canPreviewDeliveryNotePdf with isDirty/isSaving false because it has no editor. This boolean is UI state, not a new persisted field.
+
+onBack/onRetry belong to the host. onOpenShipment receives the selected note's Shipment ID only when canOpenShipment. onPreviewPdf receives Shipment ID and note ID as strings; integrate DeliveryNoteService.previewPdf without changing its authenticated GET or identity checks. No create/update/issue/cancel callbacks exist.
+
+PDF is absent for SUBMISSION_PENDING; DRAFT is disabled with the approved EN/EL explanation if movement details are unsaved; the four other statuses permit preview. A synchronous guard prevents repeat requests. Actions reset only on document/Shipment identity changes, preserving in-flight work across refreshes of the same note. Late completion after unmount cannot display an old error. Preview failure uses localized text rather than raw response contents.
+
+## Components and presentation
+
+Existing Breadcrumbs, Heading/Text, StatusPill, Button, Tabs/TabList/Tab/TabPanel, Card/CardHeader/CardBody, Table primitives, Spinner/EmptyState and Alert are used from src/components/ui. Locale comes from LabelsProvider. Heading size classes are repeated at the call site because the current cn/tailwind-merge combination drops the shared Heading's size class when text-fg follows it. No shared component change is included.
+
+Document → Movement → Goods covered; one Details tab. Render stored note lines and totals directly; never rebuild them from current Shipment goods. Recipient and addresses are the note's stored values. Fiscal number/date do not determine status. Preserve absent optional values and numeric zero. Status colors and movement-purpose/date formatting reuse current portal conventions. Fields/actions wrap for Greek and narrow screens.
+
+## Activation and ownership
+
+Before mounting, FRO-361 needs its authorized standalone read (including cancelled records), Shipment/company display data, shared saved-state context, and backend-enforced record access. UI booleans are not authorization. The list/main-navigation/search work remains outside this Details preparation and is still required by FRO-361.
+
+Do not mount the Shipment DeliveryNotesCard: it contains automatic draft preparation and mutation hooks. Do not import testing fixtures into runtime routes. Current route configuration, GraphQL documents, generated files, backend, database, theme and dependencies are unchanged.
+
+## Verification
+
+Use Node 22.13.0 and the repository dependency setup. From frontline-forwarding-client:
+
+- pnpm exec vitest run src/features/delivery-notes
+- pnpm test (lower worker concurrency may be used to diagnose machine-contention timeouts)
+- pnpm run build
+- pnpm run format:check
+- pnpm exec tsc --noEmit
+
+Tests cover layout/identity/zero values, all statuses, disabled shared draft state in EN/EL, double clicks, PDF failures/retry, stale completions, navigation and unavailable-state clearing. Fixture-only browser verification is performed outside the production tree at desktop/mobile widths. It establishes UI behavior, not live backend integration. Exact results and known baseline failures live in the planning handoff. No API/schema changes mean no reference generation is needed.
